Q: search in a sorted 2D-array (Leetcode 74)

Logic :
Think in a way that flatten 2d array (i.e, 1-D array)

find start and end pointer
start=0
end=total elements-1 (r*c-1)

while start<=end 
mid=start+(end-start)/2

find the middle element's index position
r=mid/coln
c=mid%coln
if arr[r][c] equals target
return true
if arr[r][c]<target
r=mid+1
else
c=mid-1

if target not found
return false



Code :
class Solution {
    public boolean searchMatrix(int[][] arr, int target) {
      int row=arr.length;
	    int coln=arr[0].length;
	    int low=0;
	    int high=row*coln-1;
	    while(low<=high){
	        int mid=low+(high-low)/2;
	        int r=mid/coln;
	        int c=mid%coln;
	        if(arr[r][c]==target){
	            return true;
	        }
	        if(arr[r][c]<target){
	            low=mid+1;
	        }
	        else{
	            high=mid-1;
	        }
	    }
	    return false;
    }
}
